# {{name}} installer

An Orchestration AI installer. Visitors open the install link, see a landing
page describing what will be installed, authorize with `role_admin`, pick a
workspace, and apply.

## Files

- `{{slug}}.installer.ts` — the orchestration definition (agents, layers, settings, files).
- `install.ts` — the server entrypoint (`createInstaller(...).listen()`).
- `custom-steps/` — optional HTML + server logic for third-party connections.

## Running

Set the OAuth app credentials registered for this installer:

```bash
export INSTALLER_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...
export INSTALLER_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=...
export INSTALLER_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://install.example.com/install
```

Then start it:

```bash
# Node
npx tsx install.ts

# Deno
deno run --allow-all --env-file install.ts
```

Open http://localhost:3002/ for the landing page.

## Routes

| Route | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `GET /` | Public landing page |
| `GET /install` | Install wizard (OAuth redirect target) |
| `POST /api/apply` | Runs the install (SSE progress) |
| `POST /api/uninstall` | Tears the install down |

## Uninstall

Uninstall removes the created orchestration and runs each custom step's
`uninstall` hook so third-party side effects are cleaned up.
